course: dictionary
lesson: 4984
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word independent can mean able to do things by yourself, or it can describe a country that rules itself. The words around it give you clues about which meaning to use.
explain: Look at «Most of Ireland became independent in 1922.» Ireland is a country, so independent here means ruling itself and not controlled by another country. The same word works for «an independent shop», which is not controlled by a big company.
explain: In a science test, the independent variable is the one thing you change on purpose. Change only that one thing and keep everything else the same, so you know what caused the result.
fact: Independent means able to do things without help from others, or not controlled by something else.
fact: «Independence Day» is a national holiday in the USA.
fact: «Indie» means independent: small teams or single people making games without a big company.
fact: Early Minecraft, made by Markus Persson, was an indie game.
fact: In a science fair test, the independent variable is the one thing you change on purpose.
exercise: «Most of Ireland became independent in 1922.» In this sentence, independent means | *Ruling itself, not controlled by another country | Having lots of friends | Costing a lot of money | Very tired after a long day
exercise: Mia can now dress and pack her bag by herself. Which word means she can do this without help? | Dependent | Careless | *Independent | Hungry
exercise: In a science test, what is the independent variable? | *The one thing you change on purpose | The name of the scientist | The result you measure at the end | Everything you keep the same
test: In «an independent school», what does independent mean? | Tired and sleepy | Very, very old | *Not controlled by something else | Able to swim well
test: What does «indie» mean, as in indie games? | Games played only on holiday | Games for adults only | Games with lots of loud music | *Small teams making games without a big company
exam: Which meaning of independent fits «Ella can now walk to school by herself»? | Dark and gloomy | Full of noise and fuss | Ruling a country | *Able to do things for yourself without needing help
